        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the kindest words! I already had a thought that if it was better be named 'many.nvim' :) Didn't anticipate how this project would evolve. Too late now.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, improving the \"brackets with space\" behavior is impossible under current design. Main obstacle is relying on \"balanced item\" in Lua patterns (`%b()`, for example) for \"input\" operations. It can balance only different single character left and right parts. If you are comfortable with finding not balanced pairs, try this setup (with similar values for other brackets):\r\n```lua\r\n['('] = {\r\n  input = { find = '%( .- %)', extract = '^(..).*(..)$' },\r\n  output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' },\r\n},\r\n```\r\n\r\n> Another thing I noticed is the support for tags with properties:\r\n\r\nThat is a good catch! I'll change that.\r\n",
