            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ty @echasnovski for the quick reply!\r\n\r\n>If you are comfortable with finding not balanced pairs\r\n\r\n~~What's the downside of not using balanced pairs? I tried your suggestion on a string such as `( test() )` and it still worked as expected (on the outside pairs).~~\r\n\r\n**My bad, I see the issue now, it does fail to balance the pairs when using `( test( ) )`, I don't think this is worth the hassle due to this downside.**\r\n\r\nI'm trying to come up with an `extract` pattern to handle varying amount of spaces, the below almost works, having some issues with a few edge cases, nested brackets `( ( test ) )` cause the error `(mini.surround) Could not extract two surrounding parts. Does your 'config.custom_surroundings.input.extract' pattern has two captures?`\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n    ['('] = {\r\n      input = { find = '%( .- %)', extract = '^(.%s+)[^%s]*(%s+.)$' },\r\n      output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' },\r\n    },\r\n```",
