            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What's the downside of not using balanced pairs? I tried your suggestion on a string such as ( test() ) and it still worked as expected (on the outside pairs).\r\n\r\nTry this one with cursor on `3`: `( 1 ( 2 ( 3 ) 4 ) 5 ) `\r\n\r\n> extract = '^(.%s+)[^%s]*(%s+.)$' \r\n\r\nTry either `'^(.%s+).-(%s+.)$'` or `'^(.(%s+)).-(%2.)$'` (might be wrong here, outside of my PC right now) depending on if you want to be eager or simmetrical. \r\n\r\n\r\n",
