            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "If anyone else ever needs this type of functionality this is my final version, works really well and I can now also use the left brackets to find/replace non spaced surrundings and when I need a balanced pair I use the right bracket.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n    ['('] = {\r\n      input = { find = '%(%s-.-%s-%)', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$' },\r\n      output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' },\r\n    },\r\n    ['['] = {\r\n      input = { find = '%[%s-.-%s-%]', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$' },\r\n      output = { left = '[ ', right = ' ]' },\r\n    },\r\n    ['{'] = {\r\n      input = { find = '{%s-.-%s-}', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$' },\r\n      output = { left = '{ ', right = ' }' },\r\n    },\r\n    ['<'] = {\r\n      input = { find = '<%s-.-%s->', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$' },\r\n      output = { left = '< ', right = ' >' },\r\n    },\r\n```",
