        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@ibhagwan You can set `find` to `%b()` and keep your `extract` setting, it could match balanced pairs and delete spaces with `ds` and `cs`. The full config would be:\r\n```lua\r\n    ['('] = {\r\n      input = {find = '%b()', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$'},\r\n      output = {left = '( ', right = ' )'},\r\n    },\r\n    ['['] = {\r\n      input = {find = '%b[]', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$'},\r\n      output = {left = '[ ', right = ' ]'},\r\n    },\r\n    ['{'] = {\r\n      input = {find = '%b{}', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$'},\r\n      output = {left = '{ ', right = ' }'},\r\n    },\r\n    ['<'] = {\r\n      input = {find = '%b<>', extract = '^(.%s*).-(%s*.)$'},\r\n      output = {left = '< ', right = ' >'},\r\n    },\r\n```\r\n\r\nBtw, since `%s` will match `\\n`, the matching surround  may cross lines, and mini.surround doesn't handle this situation yet. I fix it in #114.",
