        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ty for the update @echasnovski, just tested, left brackets work great by default.\r\n\r\nI do have this customization for lua style strings, is the below still the recommended way of achieving this?\r\n```lua\r\nsurround.setup({\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    S = {\r\n      -- lua bracketed string mapping\r\n      -- 'ysiwS'  foo -> [[foo]]\r\n      input = { find = '%[%[.-%]%]', extract = '^(..).*(..)$' },\r\n      output = { left = '[[', right = ']]' },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```",
