        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It should be changed. [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/085baefa6aca44526be621b15e7b688f996c2daf/doc/mini.txt#L5399) is an example.\r\n\r\nBasically, this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nsurround.setup({\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    S = {\r\n      -- lua bracketed string mapping\r\n      -- 'ysiwS'  foo -> [[foo]]\r\n      input = { '%[%[().-()%]%]' },\r\n      output = { left = '[[', right = ']]' },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSide note: I would recommend setting this only for 'lua' filetype via `vim.b.minisurround_config`. So with something like this (I put this inside 'after/ftplugin/lua.lua' file):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.b.minisurround_config = {\r\n  custom_surroundings = {\r\n    S = { input = { '%[%[().-()%]%]' }, output = { left = '[[', right = ']]' } },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```",
